# Joining a real R5 satellite at snapshot 32 as its FoF's new central (Type 1 -> 0, B:284-300).
# The halo's Mvir equals the galaxy's (B:267 not taken). The call sees Type 1 and inverts the
# written infall pair (infallVmax, infallVvir), not the current written Vmax and Vvir; the result
# equals the row's written Concentration.
# Seeded input Concentration: 6.17587757 (0x40c5a0ca), the galaxy's own written Concentration at
# the previous output snapshot (Snap_27 row 165, GalaxyIndex 1000000027, Type 0), which differs
# from the value the join stores (5.04331207, 0x40a162d0, the Snap_32 row's written value), so
# the store is visible.
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time state.
# Source: R5 reference
# /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R5/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256
# b350d5d406066b9cecf94603d5aa9597e1dcf1074015bf4edb9131bd5139d7c3), Snap_32 rows 146
# (GalaxyIndex 1000000022, Type 0) and 147 (GalaxyIndex 1000000027, Type 1, the central's
# satellite).
# SnapNum: the row stores 32; the galaxy's SnapNum 31 is a constructed call-time value and the
# halo snapshot is 32.
# Taken from the satellite row (code units): BlackHoleMass, BulgeMass, BulgeRadius, CGMgas,
# ColdGas, DiskScaleRadius, EjectedMass, H1gas, H2gas, HotGas, ICS, ICS_accrete, ICS_disrupt,
# InstabilityBulgeMass, InstabilityBulgeRadius, Len, MergerBulgeMass, MergerBulgeRadius,
# MetalsBulgeMass, MetalsCGMgas, MetalsColdGas, MetalsEjectedMass, MetalsHotGas, MetalsICS,
# MetalsStellarMass, Mvir, QuasarModeBHaccretionMass, Rvir, StellarMass, Vmax, Vvir, the infall
# record (raw); the halo catalogue's from the same row.
# Constructed (the c06 template's values): ICS_sum_mt, OutflowRate, TimeOfLastMajorMerger,
# TimeOfLastMinorMerger, the histories, deltaMvir (+2% of Mvir), Cooling and Heating (0) and the
# clock.
# Reachability: R5-reachable.
# Kind: a source-reviewed TRANSCRIPTION fixture (driver arithmetic of core_build_model.c, which
# no SAGE26 code in the oracle's link anchors), with SAGE26's own get_halo_concentration at
# B:290-295 (c12).
